# Template for /etc/darts/darts.env, which deploy/compose.yaml loads.
# bootstrap-pi.sh copies this file into place if it is not already there, and
# never overwrites an existing one -- local edits survive re-running it.
#
# Committed verbatim because there is nothing secret in here. The complete set
# of variables this process reads is filesystem paths, a port and a log level;
# the app has no authentication, no API keys and no outbound calls. If that
# ever stops being true, this file stops being committable.
#
# Every variable carries the DARTS_ prefix, which is deliberate: `env | grep
# DARTS_` inside the container is a complete inventory of how it is configured.
#
# Unset and empty mean the same thing to the app, so blank lines below are
# genuinely "use the default" -- with one exception, which is why some
# variables here are commented out rather than left blank. Compose hands
# env_file entries to the container as real environment variables, and those
# *override the image's own ENV*. A blank `DARTS_STATIC_DIR=` would therefore
# not mean "use the image default", it would override the image's
# /app/static with empty and send the app looking for frontend/dist in a
# source checkout that does not exist here. Leave those commented.

# --- Paths -----------------------------------------------------------------

# The live database, on the /var/lib/darts bind mount. The server creates the
# parent directory if it is missing, so an empty mount is fine.
DARTS_DB_PATH=/var/lib/darts/darts.db

# Where snapshots are published for the Samba share in #30.
#
# This one MUST be set explicitly. Its default is `snapshots/` *beside the
# database*, so leaving it blank would silently put snapshots in
# /var/lib/darts/snapshots and #30's share would be permanently empty --
# with nothing failing to indicate why.
DARTS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/srv/darts-share

# Deliberately left unset. The default is `backups/` beside the database,
# which resolves to /var/lib/darts/backups -- exactly where #28 wants it. Set
# it only to move backups off this disk.
#DARTS_BACKUP_DIR=

# Set by the image to /app/static. Commented, not blank: see the note above.
#DARTS_STATIC_DIR=

# --- Server ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Changing this also means changing the published port in compose.yaml;
# Compose cannot interpolate from an env_file.
DARTS_PORT=8000

DARTS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Stamped in at image build time from the commit being built, and reported by
# /api/healthz and /api/version. Commented, not blank: a blank value here
# would override the build stamp and make every image report "unknown".
#DARTS_GIT_SHA=
